<title>UK: Kwik Save full-year profits down 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Kwik Save full-year profits down 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 14.61 loss	  vs  51.68 gain</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  14.05		 vs  14.05</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  20.0		  vs  20.0</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-exceptional 90.3		  vs 125.5</p>
<p> Sales including VAT	3.512 bln	  vs   3.228 bln</p>
<p> *Exceptional item	 87.5		  vs n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptional charge relates to store closure programme of which 63.8 million is a provision for loss on disposal and  the remainder included as an exceptional item within overheads.  </p>
<p> Gross profit	    457.3		   vs 440.2</p>
<p> Operating profit	 71.5		   vs 134.1</p>
<p> Tax			  25.5		   vs  45.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 9, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 82.0 to 90.0 million stg.</p>
</text>
